{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"a208fc9881f05971","type":"text","text":"build, test, and release software faster and more reliably.","x":540,"y":99,"width":496,"height":50},
		{"id":"99058394656eae10","type":"text","text":"developers get the fast feedback they need to rapidly iterate and improve on application code","x":556,"y":24,"width":778,"height":50},
		{"id":"25dec1debe5ac8e3","type":"text","text":"make decisions and implement changes without a cumbersome and lengthy approval process.","x":614,"y":-48,"width":777,"height":50},
		{"id":"f470682989118126","type":"text","text":"Development and operations staff should both be responsible for the success or failure of a product.","x":633,"y":-117,"width":826,"height":50},
		{"id":"d4e72e12d9a25ba1","type":"text","text":"shared responsibilities","x":328,"y":-117,"width":236,"height":50},
		{"id":"ec12a157a68fcf0a","type":"text","text":"Autonomous teams","x":328,"y":-48,"width":232,"height":50},
		{"id":"1008814b3e827dcb","type":"text","text":"fast feedback","x":328,"y":24,"width":171,"height":50},
		{"id":"82e8e29cc8de7bcb","type":"text","text":"Automation","x":328,"y":99,"width":164,"height":50},
		{"id":"33ee98a9f2f5d288","type":"text","text":"culture","x":81,"y":-211,"width":123,"height":50},
		{"id":"a9502eb09c7c3472","type":"text","text":"increased transparency, communication, and collaboration between teams","x":326,"y":-186,"width":639,"height":50},
		{"id":"5c29fd52afdce3ac","type":"text","text":"DevOps culture involves closer collaboration and a shared responsibility between development and operations for the products they create and maintain.","x":328,"y":-306,"width":676,"height":60},
		{"id":"6ae6acef9ac58534","type":"text","text":"Release faster and work smarter","x":298,"y":-622,"width":310,"height":50},
		{"id":"254f35e9cd4aefae","type":"text","text":"Accelerate time-to-resolution","x":298,"y":-541,"width":288,"height":50},
		{"id":"017c1294ac45c0ec","type":"text","text":"Better manage unplanned work","x":298,"y":-476,"width":301,"height":50},
		{"id":"12cbdee9ffccb4aa","type":"text","text":"Building a culture of shared responsibility, transparency, and faster feedback","x":614,"y":-697,"width":646,"height":50},
		{"id":"3d82dbb0c160a30d","type":"text","text":"The team with the fastest feedback loop is the team that thrives. \nFull transparency and seamless communication enable DevOps teams to minimize downtime and resolve issues faster.","x":640,"y":-547,"width":961,"height":63},
		{"id":"8ec03d85b4035b16","type":"text","text":"A lack of automated test and review cycles slow the release to production.","x":656,"y":-622,"width":630,"height":50},
		{"id":"766f373a520168a5","type":"text","text":"Collaboration and trust","x":298,"y":-697,"width":251,"height":50},
		{"id":"550e5bc991f38f89","type":"text","text":"Benefits","x":81,"y":-586,"width":126,"height":50},
		{"id":"5a84f1bfddb0a20b","type":"text","text":"CI/CD","x":81,"y":364,"width":111,"height":50},
		{"id":"bb61e22221d76fe7","type":"text","text":"Continuous integration ( CI )","x":265,"y":256,"width":277,"height":50},
		{"id":"9aabf3d2e9a6a59d","type":"text","text":"continuous delivery and continuous deployment ( CD ) ","x":265,"y":389,"width":484,"height":50},
		{"id":"86d37d4303a1d07b","type":"text","text":"automating the integration of code changes from multiple contributors in a software project.","x":614,"y":256,"width":773,"height":50},
		{"id":"6eb499aad662bf7a","type":"text","text":"Continuous delivery is an organizational methodology that brings together engineering and non-engineering teams like design, product, and marketing to deliver a product.","x":850,"y":332,"width":753,"height":82},
		{"id":"0fe550d449d92980","type":"text","text":"Continuous deployment allows code changes to be automatically deployed into production when they are made, either hidden behind a feature flag, deployed to a small percentage of customers, and/or easily rolled back.","x":850,"y":439,"width":753,"height":107},
		{"id":"bda1ec1b42861d36","type":"text","text":"​​​​​​​Shift left with CI/CD","x":390,"y":690,"width":226,"height":50},
		{"id":"9a4fb125c6b8e897","type":"text","text":"Instead of sending multiple changes to a separate test or QA team, a variety of tests are performed throughout the coding process so that developers can fix bugs or improve code quality while they work on the relevant section of the codebase.","x":694,"y":685,"width":1019,"height":60},
		{"id":"7ec18878c8c11830","type":"text","text":"Agile is an iterative approach to project management and software development that helps teams deliver value to their customers faster and with fewer headaches.","x":694,"y":599,"width":713,"height":73},
		{"id":"6195823f7a0f29ad","type":"text","text":"Agile project management","x":390,"y":611,"width":268,"height":50},
		{"id":"bb364be8134c61cc","type":"text","text":"Build with the right tools","x":390,"y":764,"width":250,"height":50},
		{"id":"203420f0c1cdd552","type":"text","text":"Implement automation","x":390,"y":831,"width":238,"height":50},
		{"id":"e3ed1058f23a024a","type":"text","text":"Monitor the DevOps pipeline and applications","x":390,"y":899,"width":412,"height":50},
		{"id":"5f7255edb821420c","type":"text","text":"Observability","x":390,"y":1008,"width":177,"height":50},
		{"id":"4d2ab0f9bed0ff5f","type":"text","text":"metrics","x":651,"y":1108,"width":127,"height":50},
		{"id":"3835916e2cd61229","type":"text","text":"include CPU/RAM reservation or usage, disk space, network connectivity, and more.","x":825,"y":1108,"width":706,"height":50},
		{"id":"071dd63c251ee870","type":"text","text":"traces","x":651,"y":1033,"width":114,"height":50},
		{"id":"c697a1ffabe0c642","type":"text","text":"track the flow of logic within the application.","x":807,"y":1033,"width":400,"height":50},
		{"id":"ff02b2cc75069df3","type":"text","text":"logs","x":651,"y":965,"width":98,"height":50},
		{"id":"194d18b4872ebe75","type":"text","text":"time-series data about the functioning of the system or application.","x":807,"y":965,"width":583,"height":50},
		{"id":"1b8048fbc6ae33f5","type":"text","text":"Gather continuous feedback","x":390,"y":1188,"width":284,"height":50},
		{"id":"d01c5cf718453dbc","type":"text","text":"Change the culture","x":390,"y":1259,"width":217,"height":50},
		{"id":"45413bc78c82f697","type":"text","text":"Best Practices","x":81,"y":874,"width":192,"height":50},
		{"id":"7abaf3ab09953618","type":"text","text":"# DevOps","x":-219,"y":99,"width":175,"height":74},
		{"id":"6a07a91d4de9cbdb","x":-1617,"y":10,"width":463,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Continuous integration and continuous deployment"},
		{"id":"a11aa708f0eef71e","x":-1499,"y":79,"width":345,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"System architecture and provisioning"},
		{"id":"ef5c034c7c81a83c","x":-1472,"y":147,"width":318,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Communication and collaboration"},
		{"id":"c3768d734b6b632f","x":-1454,"y":285,"width":300,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Experience with DevOps tools"},
		{"id":"f6f5cdbcf8521d6c","x":-1424,"y":358,"width":270,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Configuration management"},
		{"id":"17401d575c8c5ef3","x":-1517,"y":429,"width":363,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Containers and container orchestration"},
		{"id":"5ef9e64c33fb311b","x":-1019,"y":172,"width":101,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"skills"},
		{"id":"872f75fd663ba925","x":-1404,"y":216,"width":250,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"System administration"},
		{"id":"56db05e44bc6e193","x":-1495,"y":498,"width":341,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Familiarity with coding and scripting"},
		{"id":"246da35dfebff82d","x":-1492,"y":575,"width":338,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Collaborative management skills"},
		{"id":"2caa13feffbc2e07","x":-594,"y":830,"width":208,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"How to do DevOps"},
		{"id":"5d90a0b0915bbc18","x":-949,"y":715,"width":207,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Pick a component"},
		{"id":"3597123e5892dccb","x":-1208,"y":780,"width":466,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Consider adopting an agile methodology like scrum"},
		{"id":"6d6c62b0b1753abf","x":-1030,"y":846,"width":288,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Use Git-based source control"},
		{"id":"406f9ca89a666676","x":-1135,"y":912,"width":393,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Integrate source control with work tracking"},
		{"id":"1409d6fe0755a16b","x":-895,"y":981,"width":153,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Write tests"},
		{"id":"e0f6dbb934435c33","x":-1195,"y":1047,"width":453,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Build out a CI/CD process to deploy the component"},
		{"id":"306baa8fe8a09fff","x":-1144,"y":1111,"width":402,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Add monitoring, alarms, and instrumentation"},
		{"id":"3c517cdd14980349","x":-1154,"y":1174,"width":412,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Use feature flags to implement canary testing"},
		{"id":"d1ce0af66d5adbcc","x":-1531,"y":-682,"width":846,"height":75,"type":"text","text":"- DevOps can be thought of as an evolution of agile practices, or as a missing piece of agile.\n- It’s an effort to take the innovations of the agile approach and apply them to operations processes."},
		{"id":"fe498516b8365204","x":-579,"y":-670,"width":193,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"DevOps vs. Agile"},
		{"id":"432c60a6bf9297d7","x":-953,"y":-455,"width":240,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"similarities/differences"},
		{"id":"6375df6c0050e97b","x":-1939,"y":-305,"width":879,"height":90,"type":"text","text":"The Agile Manifesto explicitly prioritizes individuals and interactions, working software, customer collaboration, and responding to change. These are clearly the same priorities of DevOps but extended beyond the development process and into the management of systems and running applications."},
		{"id":"b337c71fce6ccf7e","x":-2068,"y":-372,"width":1008,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Agile adds structure to planned work for developers — DevOps incorporates unplanned work common to operations teams"},
		{"id":"f800472ba10c617e","x":-2002,"y":-437,"width":942,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Agile emphasizes iterative development and small batches — DevOps focuses more on test and delivery automation"},
		{"id":"fa7c8d0ceda52b77","x":-2088,"y":-505,"width":1028,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Agile centers the flow of software from ideation to code completion — DevOps extends the focus to delivery and maintenance"},
		{"id":"9e73ce346135e364","x":-2029,"y":-574,"width":969,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Agile emphasizes collaboration between developers and product management — DevOps includes the operations team"},
		{"id":"9a0fad94e158082b","x":-1803,"y":-107,"width":885,"height":79,"type":"text","text":"A DevOps engineer is an IT generalist who should have a wide-ranging knowledge of both development and operations, including coding, infrastructure management, system administration, and DevOps toolchains."},
		{"id":"7c244788159e7b31","x":-665,"y":-157,"width":279,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"What is a DevOps engineer?"},
		{"id":"58aa8b81a103b6c0","type":"text","text":"bring these teams closer together","x":1014,"y":-186,"width":340,"height":50}
	],
